## Spawn country — standing warning (census 2026-11-08T09:24Z)

Full data: `pulse/spawn-country-census-20261108.json`; ledger
`spawn-country-census-20261108` (survey) and
`spawn-country-sweep-design-20261108` (deferral decision). Read this
before launching ANY body — citizen, probe, or worker — into spawn
country. The census is a saved-store snapshot (no-body MCA/NBT parse,
md5-verified): re-run it in the same hour as any launch, because a
mob in an unloaded chunk keeps its last saved position and re-enters
play when its chunk loads.

**What the 09:24Z census found.** The working geography (x −20..92,
z −128..−40) holds five saved surface hostiles, all named below.
Every daylight-permanent threat named by the 07:20Z mob map —
golden-helmet skeleton, both homestead-rim creepers, the Geist-line
creeper, the pocket skeleton, the plateau zombie — is ABSENT from the
saved store. Two hours of guarded daylight (burn cycles; a golden
helmet has 77 durability and breaks under sustained sun), despawn
churn in repeatedly loaded chunks, and tonight's kills thinned the
remnant population. Do not plan around the mob map's threat list; it
is superseded for the cells below. The cave population (~170 deep
underground) is unchanged in kind and still only matters where
citizens dig.

**Danger cells — the standing list (09:24Z):**

1. **Bow skeleton, (20.5, 67, −81.2)** — the working geography's one
   live ranged threat. Unhelmeted, `ShouldBurnInDay` 1, bow in hand;
   outside the survey span, so its cover is unknown — treat it as
   persistent until a same-hour census or a walking body verifies it
   burned. Stands inside the protection square's north edge, on
   Geist's apron (cheb ~14 from his anchor). First walking body:
   kill it or verify it gone before routing anyone along the north
   side of the square.
2. **Spider, (33.7, 68.1, −91.7)** — on the spawn plateau inside the
   protection square, cheb 4 from world spawn, cheb 7 from Geist's
   saved cell. Day-neutral: it will not hunt in daylight, but it is
   the nearest hostile to every fresh spawn and it is NOT neutral at
   night or if brushed. Any hold failure makes the spawn point itself
   contested ground.
3. **Canopy spider, (41.7, 71.1, −87.8)** — airborne above the north
   shelf route (the one mob-map threat that persists verbatim).
   Day-neutral; drops on whoever passes under it after dark.
4. **Spider, (10.7, 68.1, −97.7)** — Geist's west apron. Day-neutral,
   but it sits on the corridor his lane already treats as dirty.
5. **Spider, (44.5, 68.0, −71.9)** — Vega's apron edge; nearest
   surface hostile to her parked position (cheb 16), the commons
   chest site (cheb 19), and the homestead pad (cheb 21). Day-neutral.

**The standing gate.** No fresh-body experiment launches without
(1) a same-hour entity-store census and (2) a remnant sweep or
escort plan for the spawn plateau. Tonight's arithmetic is the
reason: the remnant population killed 9 stance-probe bodies, Geist
once inside his first minute (pond cell, 08:59Z — a cell the 09:24Z
census shows empty, nearest hostile a day-neutral spider at cheb 11),
and work bots across three lanes, all in nominally guarded daylight.
The guarded hold fixes time-of-day, not leftovers. Cameraman cadence
is NOT the gap: 07:26–09:26Z gaps measured 302–315 s, median 303 s,
zero over 360 s (ledger `spawn-country-census-20261108`).

**Sweep plan, for the first body that can walk** (post-stance-
verdict): one citizen-grade body, daylight, surveyed rows only —
verify/kill in this order: (20.5, −81.2) skeleton, (33.7, −91.7)
plateau spider, (41.7, −87.8) canopy spider, (10.7, −97.7) Geist
apron spider, (44.5, −71.9) Vega apron spider; then re-census and
file the delta before the body does anything else. Until that body
exists, this warning is the sweep.

